Usage of the Error Indication is specified in Section 10 of TS 38.413. Its applicabiltiy to A-IoT related NGAP function is out of question. It first would need to be made applicable for the direct connectivity option. As for the NG Setup and AMF/RAN Configuration Update procedures we suggest including verbal description that the AMF shown in the message figures and the AMF mentioned in the procedural text may be an AIOTF in case of direct connectivity option. Proposal 10: Make the Error Indication procedure applicable for direct connectivity with the AIOTF by adding verbal description that “AMF” in the Figures and the procedure text is to be regarded as an “AIOTF”. Remaining question is whether the Error Indication procedure and/or Criticality Diagnostics IE would need additional parameters to denote a specific A-IoT service operation (“A-IoT Correlation ID”) or information concerning a specific A-IoT device (“RAN A-IoT Device NGAP ID”) it is proposed to look at this topic at a later stage. Proposal 11: Postpone discussions related to additional A-IoT related IEs added to the Error Indication procedure or the Criticality Diagnostics IE.

